<title>JAPAN: Koa Oil restarts 127,000 bpd Marifu topper.</title>
<headline>Koa Oil restarts 127,000 bpd Marifu topper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koa Oil Co Ltd said it had brought a 127,000 barrel-per-day crude distillation unit at its Marifu plant in western Japan back on line on Friday.</p>
<p>The unit, which has been closed since September 13 for scheduled maintenance, is expected to reach full operations by Sunday.</p>
<p>Koa Oil is 50 percent owned by U.S. oil major Caltex Petroleum Corp, and 5.83 percent by Nippon Oil Co Ltd.</p>
<p>Caltex is owned equally by Texaco Inc and Chevron Corp.</p>
</text>
